title: "Aiyagari (1994QJE): Uninsured Idiosyncratic Risk and Aggregate Saving - Computational Implementation"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
url: "https://github.com/econ-ark/Aiyagari1994QJE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/econ-ark/Aiyagari1994QJE"
abstract: >-
  This repository replicates Table II of Aiyagari (1994), "Uninsured Idiosyncratic
  Risk and Aggregate Saving": the steady-state interest rate and aggregate saving
  rate for all 24 combinations of risk aversion and income persistence and
  volatility. It does so twice, in two Jupyter notebooks. One uses HARK's
  (Heterogeneous Agents Resources and toolKit) MarkovConsumerType; the other uses
  DolARK, dolo's extension to heterogeneous agents. Each compares its results with
  the published table. For the baseline calibration, the HARK notebook also draws
  the consumption functions, the wealth distribution and the supply of and demand
  for capital, and saves those figures and the economy's key numbers.
keywords:
  - "computational economics"
  - "heterogeneous agents"
  - "Aiyagari model"
  - "incomplete markets"
  - "precautionary saving"
  - "dynamic programming"
  - "HARK"
  - "numerical methods"
  - "macroeconomics"
